  "summary": "Today's health-tech landscape reveals significant structural challenges alongside incremental advances. A Trilliant Health report highlights how misaligned financial incentives are driving up costs and harming outcomes across the U.S. healthcare system, while regulatory and competitive pressures are mounting on multiple fronts—the Justice Department is intensifying fraud enforcement against drugmakers, the Trump administration is pursuing lower Medicare drug prices despite PhRMA's legal challenge, and proposals like a $70,000 international student work visa fee could worsen healthcare workforce shortages. On the technology side, Teladoc is expanding its virtual care platform with contactless vitals monitoring and ambient AI scribing, while investment activity remains mixed: Vitalize raised $31 million for hospital staffing solutions and General Medicine secured $120 million, but Caribou Biosciences is shutting down after failing to fund its CAR-T cell therapy trial. Regulatory uncertainty is also brewing around AI deployment, particularly in Utah's AI sandbox which may face FDA complications, and healthcare systems are increasingly focused on governance frameworks to build confidence in AI implementations across their organizations.",
